WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:01.934
[suspenseful music]

00:00:02.001 --> 00:00:03.269
 Congratulations, gentlemen.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:04.903
You've both made it to
the final round, which

00:00:05.004 --> 00:00:06.439
means you're both
one step closer

00:00:06.539 --> 00:00:08.674
to the title of Forged
in Fire Champion

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:10.243
and that check for 10 grand.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:13.045
When you came to our forge, you
used our tools and equipment.

00:00:13.112 --> 00:00:14.480
Now, we're sending
you back to your home

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:17.784
forge to forge an iconic
blade from history.

00:00:17.884 --> 00:00:19.285
Are you ready to see
what that weapon is?

00:00:19.352 --> 00:00:19.918
 Hell yeah.

00:00:19.985 --> 00:00:20.653
 I'm ready.

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:23.656
 All right.

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:24.723
The haladie.

00:00:24.790 --> 00:00:26.492
 Ooh.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:27.827
WIL WILLIS (VOICEOVER):
The haladie

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:29.662
was a fearsome
double-bladed dagger

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:31.564
created in ancient India.

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:34.267
The two recurve blades would
meet at a straight handle

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:36.936
and could be used for
slashing or stabbing.

00:00:37.036 --> 00:00:38.938
Some haladies even
featured a third blade

00:00:39.038 --> 00:00:40.540
running out of the hand guard.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.276
Though the haladie might seem
like something out of a fantasy

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:46.913
video game, it actually dates
back to the mid-fifth century

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.382
and was wielded by the
Rajput, a major Hindu

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:52.452
clan known for their bravery
and ferocity in battle.

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:58.290
 Your final challenge
is to forge a haladie.

00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:02.295
It must be an effective,
working version of that weapon.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:05.398
You will have five days at your
home forge to accomplish this.

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:08.001
Additionally, each
blade must have

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:13.706
a counter recurve and a
centered, unguarded handle.

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:15.308
At the end of five
days, you will

00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:18.177
return and present your haladies
to our panel of expert judges.

00:01:18.244 --> 00:01:19.612
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:20.946
We'll see you in five days.

00:01:21.046 --> 00:01:21.914
 Good luck, Steve.

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:25.485 line:7%
[music playing]

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:27.553
STEPHEN: Feeling amazing.

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:29.855
I made it to the finals,
and I get to make

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:31.323
a really awesome weapon--

00:01:31.423 --> 00:01:34.793
a "hal-a-die," or a "hal-i-die,"
or something like that.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:36.229
[laughs]

00:01:37.663 --> 00:01:39.932
Ray has more experience than
me, and I kind of feel like it's

00:01:39.998 --> 00:01:41.467
old school versus new school.

00:01:41.534 --> 00:01:43.670
Got my blade length
that I want to.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:45.504
Now I'm moving on the handle.

00:01:45.571 --> 00:01:48.140
Every time I hit it on
one side, the other side

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.643
bends a little bit,
so it's a challenge

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:52.245
to keep everything in line.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:56.349
Oh, yeah.

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:57.883
It's the end of day
one, and I feel like I'm

00:01:57.950 --> 00:01:59.184
a step ahead of the game.

00:01:59.284 --> 00:02:01.020
I only expected to get
forging done today,

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:03.922
but I got a little
grinding in there too.

00:02:04.023 --> 00:02:07.494 line:7%
[music playing]

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:11.330
RAY: The plan for today is
to get the Damascus ready

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.099 line:0%
and hopefully get a
couple welds in on it.

00:02:13.165 --> 00:02:14.867 line:0%
I'm going to cut up a
bunch of steel here.

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:16.435 line:7%
I used a 15-piece billet.

00:02:16.502 --> 00:02:18.804 line:0%
I've never made a haladie,
and I've never made

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.239
a double-ended knife either.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:21.641
To me, it's a challenge.

00:02:21.707 --> 00:02:23.209
Challenge is good.

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:26.012
Even though I've got,
like, 37 years experience,

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:27.546
it's not going to be easy.

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:30.817
[music playing]

00:02:32.251 --> 00:02:34.119
I'm going to go for,
like, 120 layers.

00:02:34.186 --> 00:02:35.454
It'll give me a
bold pattern, and I

00:02:35.554 --> 00:02:36.823
think it'll look really nice.

00:02:41.193 --> 00:02:42.395 line:7%
STEPHEN: It's day two.

00:02:42.461 --> 00:02:44.964
I've got pretty much
all the grinding done.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.767
Today I want to get
to the heat treating.

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:51.771
That's the make-it-or-break-it
part of the knife.

00:02:51.837 --> 00:02:55.741
This is my first time having
this much riding on the quench.

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:58.111
I hope nothing goes
wrong, 'cause if it does,

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:01.014
I'll have to restart, and
that would really suck.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:04.551
[suspenseful music]

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:10.589
It survived.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.658
Feeling good.

00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:15.428
Now I just gotta do the same
thing to the other side.

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.398 line:7%
RAY: Ready to start day three.

00:03:19.498 --> 00:03:20.966 line:0%
I wish I was a
little farther ahead,

00:03:21.033 --> 00:03:22.702
but everything is times two.

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:24.437
So whatever I do to
one blade, it has to be

00:03:24.503 --> 00:03:26.105
exactly like the other blade.

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:30.142
And that can be a
challenge in itself.

00:03:30.242 --> 00:03:32.878
So I put the first
blade in the jig,

00:03:32.945 --> 00:03:34.480
and I can't get it to bend.

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:36.248
So I said, I'm gonna do
it the old school way

00:03:36.315 --> 00:03:37.884
and go back to the anvil.

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:40.219
So it's just going
to be a guess.

00:03:40.285 --> 00:03:42.054
Whenever you're
dealing with Damascus,

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.222
it's a risky business.

00:03:43.288 --> 00:03:44.723
And it doesn't always
turn out right.

00:03:44.823 --> 00:03:46.993
Nobody makes perfect Damascus
every time they make it.

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:51.030
This is about a wicked looking
weapon, I'll tell you what.

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:54.166 line:7%
[music playing]

00:03:54.233 --> 00:03:55.568
STEPHEN: It's day
four, and pretty

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:57.903
much all I got left to
do is glue on the handle,

00:03:58.004 --> 00:03:59.338
polish that up.

00:03:59.405 --> 00:04:01.774
Ray is probably doing
Damascus with his blade,

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:03.776
so I'm trying to be
on the same level.

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.278
I'm going to hand-sand.

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:07.580
I'm going to add filework
on both sides of the handle.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.350
I'm doing, like, the
really fine detail stuff.

00:04:11.417 --> 00:04:14.553
I'm going for, like, a vine
pattern on the filework

00:04:14.654 --> 00:04:16.021
just to give it
an elegant design,

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:17.389
a little something extra.

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:20.425
I'm kind of just gonna
freeball it on this one.

00:04:20.525 --> 00:04:22.395
It's just about ready to glue.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:28.934
As soon as I start mixing the
epoxy, time starts going down.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.970
I only got five minutes to
get everything where I want

00:04:31.036 --> 00:04:32.405
it to be because of the epoxy.

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:38.911
This is the first bump in
the road I've run into,

00:04:38.978 --> 00:04:41.781
and I feel the time crunch.

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:43.182
OK.

00:04:43.249 --> 00:04:45.884
I finally get it together.

00:04:45.984 --> 00:04:50.356
The glue's all set up, and it
looks like there's no gaps.

00:04:50.423 --> 00:04:52.491
I finished the
weapon a day early.

00:04:52.591 --> 00:04:54.961
There's always that thought
in the back of my head

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:56.562
where I'm going
against the best.

00:04:56.629 --> 00:04:59.464
But age definitely
doesn't limit your skill.

00:04:59.564 --> 00:05:00.767
I'm very proud of this weapon.

00:05:03.336 --> 00:05:04.070 line:7%
RAY: Last day.

00:05:04.136 --> 00:05:05.270
It's crunch time.

00:05:05.337 --> 00:05:06.505
Time to finish it up.

00:05:06.605 --> 00:05:08.207
The heat treat went
really well yesterday,

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:10.109
and the blades look good.

00:05:10.176 --> 00:05:11.410
First thing I'm
going to do today

00:05:11.476 --> 00:05:13.379
is sharpen the blades
up before I assemble

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.748
the bond to the handle.

00:05:15.815 --> 00:05:19.952
I think my skill set as a
mastersmith really shows up.

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:21.520
I came here to
prove that I could

00:05:21.620 --> 00:05:24.390
compete at a really high level,
and I think that I did that.

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:25.891
The only thing
that could stop it

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:29.195
is if my competitor built
something better than I did.

00:05:29.295 --> 00:05:31.064
I think it's ready to go.

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:34.600
[suspenseful music]

00:05:35.734 --> 00:05:38.104
 Stephen, Ray, welcome
back to the forge.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:40.105
You've had five days
at your home forges

00:05:40.172 --> 00:05:41.807
to work on your haladies.

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:44.076
Now it's time to see how they
hold up in our weapons test.

00:05:44.143 --> 00:05:47.813
But first, Ray, tell us a
little bit about your weapon.

00:05:47.913 --> 00:05:51.250 line:0%
 Well, I made my haladie
as close as I could

00:05:51.350 --> 00:05:53.352 line:7%
to the original type of weapon.

00:05:53.418 --> 00:05:55.521 line:0%
And I made the blades
out of Damascus,

00:05:55.588 --> 00:05:57.857 line:7%
and I think it'll do well.

00:05:57.924 --> 00:05:58.657 line:7%
 OK.

00:05:58.757 --> 00:06:00.193 line:7%
Stephen, tell us about yours.

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:02.694 line:0%
 I forged mine out of
1095 high-carbon steel

00:06:02.761 --> 00:06:05.163 line:0%
and put my own kind
of twist on it from

00:06:05.230 --> 00:06:07.800 line:7%
stuff I saw on the internet.

00:06:07.867 --> 00:06:08.901
 All right, gentlemen.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:10.670
Your weapons will now
be put through a series

00:06:10.737 --> 00:06:11.938
of three tests.

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:15.040
Up first is the sharpness test.

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.275
Doug?

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:18.010
 Bladesmiths, the
haladie was a weapon

00:06:18.110 --> 00:06:19.612
used by the Rajput warriors.

00:06:19.678 --> 00:06:21.814
It was designed to have a blade
on both sides of the handle,

00:06:21.881 --> 00:06:23.883
and they were known
to be very sharp.

00:06:23.949 --> 00:06:26.652
To see how sharp your weapons
are, I will take your blade

00:06:26.752 --> 00:06:30.489
and deliver multiple cuts
and stabs to this canvas bag.

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:31.624
Ray, you're up first.

00:06:31.691 --> 00:06:32.324
You ready?

00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:33.192
 I'm ready.

00:06:33.259 --> 00:06:33.793
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:06:36.695 --> 00:06:38.030
RAY: I'm really
proud of this knife.

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:39.565
I mean, it turned
out really well.

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:41.867
The curvature on the
blade is a recurve,

00:06:41.967 --> 00:06:44.270
so what happens is the blade
starts in one direction

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:46.438
then comes back in the
other direction, which

00:06:46.505 --> 00:06:48.708
gives it a lot of character.

00:06:48.775 --> 00:06:52.044
[music playing]

00:06:59.085 --> 00:07:00.452
 OK, Ray.

00:07:00.552 --> 00:07:02.288
I like the design of your blade.

00:07:02.388 --> 00:07:03.622
It feels good in the hand.

00:07:03.689 --> 00:07:05.891
You got that ovoid
shape for the handle.

00:07:05.991 --> 00:07:07.960
And I like also how
it flares over there,

00:07:08.027 --> 00:07:10.430
so it stops for the thrust.

00:07:10.496 --> 00:07:14.066
I love your recurve and
Damascus pattern that you have

00:07:14.166 --> 00:07:16.169
on both ends of your blade.

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:19.572
It's very dramatic,
and it looks good.

00:07:19.638 --> 00:07:24.777
The belly of your blade
slashed nicely on the canvas,

00:07:24.844 --> 00:07:27.412
and it allowed
for a good thrust.

00:07:27.479 --> 00:07:30.149
And this blade will cut.

00:07:30.249 --> 00:07:30.949
Good job.

00:07:31.016 --> 00:07:31.917
 Thank you.

00:07:32.017 --> 00:07:33.385
 Stephen, you're up next.
You ready?

00:07:33.452 --> 00:07:34.253
 Hell yeah.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.721
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:38.658
[music playing]

00:07:39.925 --> 00:07:41.493
STEPHEN: Going up against
a master bladesmith

00:07:41.593 --> 00:07:43.696
with 30 years'
experience is definitely

00:07:43.762 --> 00:07:45.264
a little nerve-racking for me.

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:47.934
But I'm pretty sure
I got everything

00:07:48.034 --> 00:07:49.135
executed perfectly on it.

00:07:54.106 --> 00:07:59.879
 Well, Stephen, we
have a big problem here.

00:07:59.946 --> 00:08:01.046
 What's the problem?

00:08:01.147 --> 00:08:08.220
 We specifically asked for
a recurve on each blade.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:12.925
These blades are not recurve.

00:08:12.992 --> 00:08:14.793
They're simply curved.

00:08:14.893 --> 00:08:16.795
We put that specifically
on the parameters

00:08:16.862 --> 00:08:19.031
so that both blades
are equal and fair

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:20.966
in all the tests that we do.

00:08:21.066 --> 00:08:24.069
Your blade does not have
that S-shape recurve

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:25.171
that we're looking for.

00:08:27.907 --> 00:08:30.509
Because you don't have that
S-shape recurve that we

00:08:30.575 --> 00:08:32.277
needed for the
parameters, we cannot

00:08:32.344 --> 00:08:33.613
move on to test your blade.

00:08:36.081 --> 00:08:39.551
 Well, Stephen, the
devil's in the details.

00:08:39.651 --> 00:08:41.720
The blade parameters
were very specific.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:45.223
We asked for counter recurve
blades on your haladie.

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:46.692
You didn't deliver that.

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:48.527
Therefore, since
your weapon cannot be

00:08:48.593 --> 00:08:51.563
tested fairly and
evenly, I must ask

00:08:51.663 --> 00:08:52.865
you to please leave the forge.

00:08:57.636 --> 00:08:58.737
 I'm feeling a little bummed.

00:08:58.837 --> 00:08:59.738
I put in all that
hard work and then

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:01.073
didn't even get to test it.

00:09:01.140 --> 00:09:02.875
I still feel really
proud of my work.

00:09:02.942 --> 00:09:07.413
It's just I failed to see
that one small detail,

00:09:07.513 --> 00:09:10.883
and that led me to losing.

00:09:10.949 --> 00:09:15.754
I learned I gotta follow the
instructions a little better.

00:09:15.821 --> 00:09:17.322
 Ray, congratulations.

00:09:17.423 --> 00:09:18.623
You are the Forged
in Fire Champion

00:09:18.723 --> 00:09:20.826
and will be receiving
a check for $10,000.

00:09:20.926 --> 00:09:21.393
Good job.

00:09:21.493 --> 00:09:23.929
[applause]

00:09:24.029 --> 00:09:24.897
 Thank you.

00:09:24.964 --> 00:09:27.599
 It's a good
looking weapon, sir.

00:09:27.666 --> 00:09:28.767
 Thank you.

00:09:28.867 --> 00:09:30.302
DOUG: I love your
Damascus pattern.

00:09:30.369 --> 00:09:32.337
Really, really nice recurve
through it, beautiful shape.

00:09:32.404 --> 00:09:34.006
WIL: How you feel right now?

00:09:34.073 --> 00:09:35.140
 Feeling really good.

00:09:35.241 --> 00:09:38.143
Being Forged in Fire
Champion, it's really nice,

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:39.544
especially at my age.

00:09:39.611 --> 00:09:41.581
I'd have felt a
lot better about it

00:09:41.647 --> 00:09:43.983
if they could've did the
cutting contest and everything

00:09:44.050 --> 00:09:45.351
with his blade also.

00:09:45.451 --> 00:09:48.520
But I just sold a
knife for 10,000 bucks.

00:09:48.587 --> 00:09:49.555
That's the best part.

00:09:49.622 --> 00:09:52.992
[music playing]

